  "notes": "This release has [l264111] lacquer cuts on both sides. \nOther Canadian releases have [l700568], [l426483] or [l278261] lacquer cuts, sometimes in combination with a Masterdisk lacquer cut on another side.\n\nReleased with a double-sided printed cardboard inner sleeve containing lyrics, photos and credits.\n\nPressed by is uncredited and is identified by a 1.5\" pressing ring on the labels.\n\nRunouts are etched apart from \"MASTERDISK,\" which is stamped.\n\nOn the back cover:\nAnthem Records\nManufactured by Anthem Records of Canada.\nDistributed by Capitol Records-EMI of Canada Limited.\n\nOn the labels:\nPublished by CORE Music Publishing (ASCAP) CAPAC Canada.\n©, ℗ 1981 Cat Productions Ltd. \nDistributed by Capitol Records-EMI of Canada Limited.\n\nOn the inner sleeve:\nRecorded and mixed at Le Studio, Morin Heights, Quebec, during October and November, of 1980\nMastered at Masterdisk, N.Y.C.\nAll lyrics © 1981, CORE Music Publishing (ASCAP) CAPAC, Canada\n© ℗ 1981 Cat Productions Ltd.\nAll music by CORE Music Publishing (ASCAP) CAPAC, Canada\n\nOn the spine:\n[Shorewood logo] Litho in Canada",
  "released_formatted": "12 Feb 1981",
